            "is_private": false,
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Created attachment 4164\npatch v2: MOD_ITERATE2 only (against r90971)\n\nApologies for a second patch version so soon after the first: I filed this before timing the patch on x86_64, which I should have done first.\n\nThe gains are smaller there: comparisons run 1.5 to 1.7 times as fast with GCC at `-O2` (tables are in the PR description). The `MOD_ITERATE1` users (`pmin()`, subassignment) turned out 10 to 17% slower, so the attached patch leaves `MOD_ITERATE1` alone and changes `MOD_ITERATE2` only. I'll explore changes to `MOD_ITERATE1` in a separate PR.\n\n\"Results do not change\" also needs a qualification on x86_64: a few results differ in whether a missing element comes out as `NA` or as `NaN` (complex arithmetic, and `NA_integer_` meeting a `NaN` double); the numbers are the same. As `?NA` says, which of the two is not guaranteed and depends on the compiler.\n\nI have no further changes planned for this patch.",
